# AI Working Rules

Before coding:
- inspect existing files
- understand current structure
- follow existing naming and patterns
- avoid rewriting unrelated code

When making changes:
- keep changes focused
- do not break existing APIs
- do not remove existing features without asking
- prefer incremental implementation
- add types for all new code
- handle errors properly
- keep tenant isolation in mind

After coding:
- explain what changed
- mention files changed
- mention commands to run
- mention any migration needed
- mention any env variable added

If unsure:
- make a safe assumption
- add a clear TODO
- do not invent fake package APIs

For every frontend change, ensure the UI is fully responsive on mobile, tablet, laptop, and desktop.
